  "description": "ONITIS crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C136 H198 Dy4 N10 Na4 Ni8 O56,10(C1 H4 O1),33(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Ni1 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni4 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Ni5 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni6 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni7 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni8 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 17 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately linear metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.018-3.593 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 90.92-108.27°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ni8Dy4Na4(OH)2(L)6(HL)2(L')2(tea)2(H2O)6(CH3OH)4]·10CH3OH·33H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 tea (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
